          "details": [],
          "source": "user-story:docs/beacon/v1.4.7/user-story/beacon-v1.4.7-bounded-automation-closure-state-kernel.md"
        },
        {
          "id": "AC-003",
          "kind": "ac",
          "theme": "QA 能稳定写出 `ready_for_release` / `implement_repair` / `human_escalation` 三类 authoritative exit intent",
          "text": "Beacon freezes a bounded next-route taxonomy that can at minimum distinguish `qa`, `implement`, `release`, and `human` for the current slice, without implying that `deep/refreeze` automation is already runtime-ready.",
          "required": true,
          "status": "draft",
          "implemented_by_run_id": null,
          "verified_by_run_id": null,
          "accepted_at": null,
          "changed_in_revision": null,
          "story_id": "",
          "details": [],
          "source": "user-story:docs/beacon/v1.4.7/user-story/beacon-v1.4.7-bounded-automation-closure-state-kernel.md"
        },
        {
          "id": "AC-004",
          "kind": "ac",
          "theme": "Implement repair 能稳定写出回到 QA 或升级人工的 exit intent",
          "text": "Beacon defines an active issue register inheritance contract so repeated repair rounds carry only still-relevant stop reasons, accepted fixes, targeted rerun hints, and prior-round references rather than copying full artifact history.",
          "required": true,
          "status": "draft",
          "implemented_by_run_id": null,
          "verified_by_run_id": null,
          "accepted_at": null,
          "changed_in_revision": null,
          "story_id": "",
          "details": [],
          "source": "user-story:docs/beacon/v1.4.7/user-story/beacon-v1.4.7-bounded-automation-closure-state-kernel.md"
        },
        {
          "id": "AC-005",
          "kind": "ac",
          "theme": "Queue writes 具备 revision 校验，stale writer 会被拒绝",
          "text": "Beacon makes QA exit authoritative for bounded runtime routing, so a QA round can explicitly emit `ready_for_release`, `implement_repair`, or `human_escalation` intent into the automation runtime object.",
          "required": true,
          "status": "draft",
          "implemented_by_run_id": null,
          "verified_by_run_id": null,
          "accepted_at": null,
          "changed_in_revision": null,
          "story_id": "",
          "details": [],
          "source": "user-story:docs/beacon/v1.4.7/user-story/beacon-v1.4.7-bounded-automation-closure-state-kernel.md"
        },
        {
          "id": "AC-006",
          "kind": "ac",
          "theme": "同一 feature 不能被两个 automation worker 同时 claim",
          "text": "Beacon makes implement repair exit authoritative for bounded runtime routing, so a repair round can explicitly emit either return-to-QA intent or human-escalation intent.",
          "required": true,
          "status": "draft",
          "implemented_by_run_id": null,
          "verified_by_run_id": null,
          "accepted_at": null,
          "changed_in_revision": null,
          "story_id": "",
          "details": [],
          "source": "user-story:docs/beacon/v1.4.7/user-story/beacon-v1.4.7-bounded-automation-closure-state-kernel.md"
        },
        {
          "id": "AC-007",
          "kind": "ac",
          "theme": "bounded runtime 仍保持 support-plane 身份，不扩张成新的 lifecycle stage",
          "text": "Beacon adds queue revision semantics so automation queue mutation is guarded against stale writers and does not silently overwrite newer queue state.",
          "required": true,
          "status": "draft",
          "implemented_by_run_id": null,
          "verified_by_run_id": null,
          "accepted_at": null,
          "changed_in_revision": null,
